[
  {"comment": "Ten blur layers over a large document, measured before the cache. A document of 3,840 by 2,160 whose Layer 1 is filled and crossed by three strokes, ten adjustment layers above it each carrying a Gaussian blur, radius 2 at the bottom of the stack and 20 at its top, and a paint layer called Above over them all. Three windows are measured, each a perf block the state dump after it keeps: a stroke on Layer 1 under the stack, a stroke on Above over it, and Above hidden by a click on its eye in the Layers docker, which is the toggle. The eye is clicked rather than the layer step used, because that step folds the caches a second time and so measures a rebuild the painter never pays. Layer thumbnails wait for the pen to lift, since their quarter second throttle reads the wall clock and would make the counts differ between two runs. Above is shown again after the third window, and the last shot is the canvas with the whole stack as it stands, the record the gate reads."},
  {"args": ["--machine-console"]},
  {"wait": 30},
  {"prefs": {"thumbnails_while_painting": "pen_lift"}},
  {"wait": 5},
  {"docker": "park"},
  {"tool": "brush"},
  {"canvas": [3840, 2160]},
  {"wait": 5},
  {"fit": true},
  {"wait": 5},
  {"fill": [0.8, 0.35, 0.2]},
  {"wait": 10},
  {"brush": {"radius": 0.04}},
  {"colour": "#2050c0"},
  {"stroke": {"from": [300, 300], "to": [3500, 1800], "pressure": 1.0, "steps": 64, "space": "document"}},
  {"wait": 5},
  {"colour": "#f0e8d0"},
  {"stroke": {"from": [300, 1800], "to": [3500, 300], "pressure": 1.0, "steps": 64, "space": "document"}},
  {"wait": 5},
  {"colour": "#101010"},
  {"stroke": {"from": [300, 1080], "to": [3500, 1080], "pressure": 1.0, "steps": 64, "space": "document"}},
  {"wait": 10},
  {"docker": {"id": "LayersDocker", "at": [1480, 120], "size": [420, 560]}},
  {"wait": 20},

